## Competitor Landscape

Competitor: Compound
Category: Decentralized Lending (Blue-chip)
Difference: Compound V3 single-asset supply markets; Aave multi-asset pools with isolation modes, flash loans, GHO stablecoin, institutional products (Arc/Horizon), V4 hub-and-spoke
Market Segment: Ethereum-mainnet focused; migrating to Compound V3; smaller multi-chain footprint
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/compound
https://compound.finance

Competitor: MakerDAO (Spark Protocol)
Category: Decentralized Lending / CDP + Lending
Difference: Maker/Spark uses DAI/USDS stablecoin backing, PSM, SparkLend for lending; Aave uses pooled lending with native GHO stablecoin, flash loans, broader multi-chain deployment
Market Segment: RWA-heavy (Maker); Spark growing on Ethereum/L2s
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/makerdao
https://defillama.com/protocol/spark

Competitor: Morpho
Category: Decentralized Lending (Peer-to-Pool Optimization)
Difference: Morpho optimizes supply/borrow rates via peer-to-peer matching on top of pools (Morpho Blue); Aave is native pooled with V4 hub-and-spoke; Morpho newer, faster-growing TVL but smaller absolute
Market Segment: Rate-optimized lending; growing on Ethereum, Base
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/morpho
https://morpho.org

Competitor: Euler
Category: Decentralized Lending (Modular, Permissionless)
Difference: Euler V2 modular vault-based lending with custom risk curves; Aave V4 hub-and-spoke with governance-managed risk; Euler younger, smaller TVL
Market Segment: Modular lending; Ethereum + L2s
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/euler
https://euler.finance

Competitor: Venus Protocol
Category: Decentralized Lending (BNB Chain Native)
Difference: Venus dominant on BNB Chain; Aave multi-chain leader; Venus uses VAI stablecoin; Aave uses GHO
Market Segment: BNB Chain focused; expanding to other chains
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/venus
https://venus.io

Competitor: Radiant Capital
Category: Decentralized Lending (Cross-Chain, LayerZero)
Difference: Radiant built on LayerZero for native cross-chain lending; Aave V4 uses CCIP/hub-and-spoke; Radiant smaller TVL, single protocol instance
Market Segment: Omnichain lending; Arbitrum, BNB Chain, Ethereum
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/radiant
https://radiant.capital

Competitor: Benqi
Category: Decentralized Lending (Avalanche Native)
Difference: Benqi dominant on Avalanche; Aave V3/V4 deployed on Avalanche; Benqi has liquid staking (sAVAX); Aave broader multi-chain
Market Segment: Avalanche focused
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/benqi
https://benqi.fi

Competitor: Gearbox
Category: Decentralized Leverage / Credit Account
Difference: Gearbox provides leverage via credit accounts; Aave provides standard overcollateralized lending; Gearbox composes on top of Aave/others
Market Segment: Leverage/strategies; Ethereum, Arbitrum
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/gearbox
https://gearbox.fi

Competitor: Notional
Category: Fixed-Rate Lending
Difference: Notional specializes in fixed-rate/fixed-term lending via fCash; Aave V3 variable/stable rates, V4 adding fixed-rate via Spokes/Stable Vaults; Notional smaller TVL
Market Segment: Fixed-rate term lending; Ethereum, Arbitrum, Optimism
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/notional
https://notional.finance

Competitor: Silo Finance
Category: Isolated Market Lending
Difference: Silo uses isolated silos per asset (risk isolation); Aave V3 isolation mode + V4 Spokes for isolation; Silo permissionless market creation; Aave governance-managed
Market Segment: Isolated/permissionless markets; Ethereum, Arbitrum, Optimism, Base
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/silo
https://silo.finance

## Narrative Position

Narrative: Blue-Chip DeFi / Money Market Leader
Status: Main Narrative
Evidence: Largest lending TVL across chains; $2.21B cumulative fees; institutional adoption via Arc/Horizon; DAO governance maturity
Sources:
https://defillama.com/protocol/aave
https://tokenterminal.com/terminal/projects/aave
https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/04/13/aave-passes-landmark-vote-ending-months-long-fight-over-who-controls-protocol-revenue/

Narrative: Real World Assets (RWA) / Institutional DeFi
Status: Main Narrative
Evidence: Aave Horizon (RWA lending market on v3.3); Aave Arc (permissioned KYC/AML); Project Guardian (MAS Singapore); Kraken white-label V3; Franklin Templeton/VanEck/Ripple mentioned as potential partners
Sources:
https://aave.com (Phase 2 L5-L8, L12-L14)
https://www.aave.org (Phase 2 L16-L17)
https://coinmarketcap.com (Phase 2 L33-L36)
https://www.xt.com (Phase 2 L24-L25)

Narrative: Native Stablecoin (GHO)
Status: Secondary Narrative
Evidence: GHO live since July 2023; $185M circulating; over-collateralized; revenue-generating for DAO; reduced borrow rates for stkAAVE stakers
Sources:
https://defillama.com/stablecoins/gho
https://www.theblock.co/post/240297/aave-protocol-activates-gho-stablecoin-on-the-ethereum-mainnet (Phase 3 EV-024)

Narrative: Cross-Chain Interoperability / Hub-and-Spoke Architecture
Status: Main Narrative (V4)
Evidence: Aave V4 hub-and-spoke with Chainlink CCIP; deployed Ethereum + Avalanche; isolates risk per Spoke; consolidates liquidity in Hubs
Sources:
https://aave.com/docs/aave-v4 (Phase 4)
https://www.kucoin.com/news/en/aave-v4-deploys-to-the-avalanche-network-with-hub-and-spoke-architecture-57916 (Phase 3 EV-032)

Narrative: Security-First Development / Formal Verification
Status: Secondary Narrative
Evidence: $1.5M security program; 345 cumulative audit days; Certora formal verification from design; 900+ researchers Sherlock contest; zero critical/high findings
Sources:
https://www.aave.com/blog/aave-v4-security-by-design (Phase 4)
https://www.gate.com (Phase 2 L22-L25)

Narrative: Governance Decentralization / DAO Maturity
Status: Main Narrative
Evidence: Aave Will Win proposal passed (75% support, $42.5M + 75k AAVE funding); Aligned Delegates Framework proposed; Orbit Program compensating delegates; Aave Foundation proposed for IP/brand
Sources:
https://finance.yahoo.com/news/aave-ends-month-long-wait-for-protocol-control-in-decisive-vote-180000698.html (Phase 3 EV-029)
https://governance.aave.com (Phase 6)
