## Summary

Market Stage: Mature
Primary Category: Decentralized Lending / Liquidity Protocol
Competitor Count: 10+ direct lending competitors (Compound, Maker/Spark, Morpho, Euler, Venus, Radiant, Benqi, Gearbox, Notional, Silo)
Major Narrative: Blue-Chip DeFi Leader; RWA/Institutional DeFi; Cross-Chain Hub-and-Spoke (V4); Native Stablecoin (GHO); Security-First; DAO Governance Maturity
Trading Availability: Spot on 10+ major CEXs (Binance, Coinbase, Kraken, OKX, Bybit, HTX, Gate.io, KuCoin); Perpetuals on 7+ CEXs; Deep DEX liquidity (Uniswap V3 multi-chain)
Adoption Metrics Available: TVL ($22.4B aggregate), Daily Users (~45k), Daily Txns (~180k), Cumulative Wallets (~1.2M), Revenue ($773.6M annualized fees), GHO Supply ($185M), stkAAVE Staked (~3.2M AAVE), Developer Count (120+)

## Open Threads

TVL Post-Exploit Recovery: TVL dropped ~$6.6B after rsETH exploit (May 2026); current $22.4B suggests recovery but exact timeline and composition (net new vs. market rebound) not verified from primary source.

Market Share Precision: DefiLlama lending category TVL includes protocols with different architectures (CDP, peer-to-pool, isolated); "lending protocol" share definition varies. Need standardized segment definition.

CEX Volume Aggregation: 24h combined spot volume ~$1.5B cited from aggregated sources; no single verified real-time feed covering all venues.

Daily Active Users Definition: "Unique depositors/borrowers" vs "unique transacting addresses" vs "unique wallet connections" — methodology differs across Dune dashboards, Token Terminal, and internal Aave analytics.

GHO Adoption Metrics: GHO supply $185M reported; but borrow volume, peg stability deviations, and minter distribution (Facilitators vs. Aave V3) not fully documented in verified public dashboards.

Competitor TVL Comparisons: Morpho TVL growing rapidly (~$3.5B per DefiLlama July 2026); Euler V2, Silo, Radiant gaining share. Relative growth rates vs. Aave not quantified in verified comparative analysis.

Institutional Adoption Quantification: Aave Horizon TVL, Arc participant count, Kraken white-label volume — specific numbers not publicly disclosed in verified format.

Aave V4 Adoption Rate: V4 launched March 2026 (Ethereum) and July 2026 (Avalanche); migration from V3, Spoke utilization rates, Hub capital efficiency metrics not yet available in public dashboards.

Bad Debt Resolution: rsETH exploit bad debt ($124-230M range) resolution across Kelp, LayerZero, Aave DAO — final allocation and recovery timeline not concluded.

Token Buyback Mechanics: $50M/year buyback program active; but whether tokens are burned, sent to treasury, or recycled as incentives — conflicting reports (Phase 6 Open Threads). Exact mechanism impacts supply dynamics.

Valuation Metrics: No traditional valuation (P/E, P/S) for protocol; Token Terminal provides P/F (Price/Fees) but methodology for "net revenue to token holders" vs "DAO revenue" differs.

Geographic User Distribution: On-chain protocol; no KYC for main markets. Geographic adoption (US vs. EU vs. Asia vs. LatAm) inferred from chain deployment density, not measured.

Developer Retention: 120+ monthly active contributors reported; but breakdown between Aave Labs employees, BGD Labs, grant recipients, and independent contributors not verified.

Security Budget Sustainability: $1.5M V4 security program funded; ongoing bug bounty, formal verification, audit costs for future upgrades — long-term funding source (DAO grants vs. protocol revenue allocation) not documented.

Regulatory Risk Exposure: Aave Arc (KYC), Horizon (RWA), Project Guardian (MAS) — evolving regulatory landscape (MiCA, US stablecoin bills, DeFi protocol classification) impact on protocol operations not quantified.

Lens Protocol Spinoff Impact: Lens spun out from Avara; Aave DAO/Aave Labs relationship with Lens (token economics, shared infrastructure, brand) not fully defined post-Avara sunset.